          "id": "ch-4-glossary-of-key-terms-unit-2",
          "number": "4",
          "title": "Glossary of Key Terms — Unit 2",
          "markdown": "## 4. Glossary of Key Terms — Unit 2\n* **Co-existence (`Sah-astitva`):** Both `Self (I)` and `Body` staying together seamlessly in mutual relationship, sharing information while remaining distinct in nature and needs.\n* **Self (`I` / Sentient Entity):** Conscious internal entity experiencing feelings, thoughts, imagination, and awareness; the Seer, Doer, and Enjoyer.\n* **Body (`Sharira`):** Physical biological structure composed of material atoms acting as the operational instrument (`Sadhan`) of the Self.\n* **Quantitative Need:** Physical facility measurable in fixed units (`calories, liters, meters`) required in finite limits (`Body`).\n* **Qualitative Need:** Inner emotional/value states (`respect, trust, harmony`) experienced continuously without physical weight (`Self`).\n* **Seer (`Drashta`), Doer (`Karta`), Enjoyer (`Bhokta`):** Three classic UHV descriptions confirming the conscious `Self (I)` observes reality, takes choices, and feels resulting satisfaction/sorrow—not the physical hands or eyes alone.\n* **Self-Regulation (`Sanyam`):** Inner responsibility assumed by the `Self` toward nurturing (`Poshan`), protecting (`Sanrakshan`), and rightly utilizing (`Sadupyog`) the Body.\n* **Health (`Svasthya`):** State where the Body acts harmoniously according to the Self (`I`) and its organs coordinate smoothly in natural order.\n* **Mutual Happiness:** Resulting satisfaction shared by both people when human–human behavior rests on Right Feelings.\n* **Mutual Prosperity:** Resulting well-being shared by humans and rest of nature when production fulfills assessed needs sustainably."
