          "markdown": "## 3. Glossary of Key Terms — Unit 3\n* **Justice (*Nyaya*):** Recognition of values in human relationship, their fulfillment, right evaluation, and mutual happiness.\n* **Trust (*Vishwas*):** Assurance that the other person naturally intends both their own and my happiness & prosperity.\n* **Intention vs. Competence:** Inherent wish for harmony (*Intention*, universally positive) vs. present practical ability to live harmoniously (*Competence*, which may lag).\n* **Respect (*Samman*):** Right evaluation of a human being based on the `Self (I)`—free from over-evaluation, under-evaluation, or differentiation.\n* **Differentiation (*Bhedbhav*):** Disrespectful discrimination judging humans unequally by Body traits, money, position, or beliefs.\n* **Affection, Care, Guidance, Reverence, Glory, Gratitude, Love:** The complete nine-value relationship spectrum balancing emotional kinship, physical protection, mental mentoring, honor for excellence, appreciation, and universal connectedness.\n* **Fearlessness (*Abhay*):** Societal trust where citizens feel safe around peers and institutions without crime, prejudice, or exploitation.\n* **Undivided Society (*Akhand Samaj*):** Human community free from divisive race/wealth/sect barriers (\"One Human World Family\"), emerging naturally from family Justice.\n* **Five Dimensions of Human Order:** *Education–Sanskar*, *Health–Sanyam*, *Production–Work*, *Justice–Preservation*, and *Exchange–Storage* sustaining societal harmony."
